hadiths[140]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3910","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife. She was menstruating at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) went to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about this. The Prophet (PBUH) said that he should go back to this woman and let her remain like that until she becomes pure. Let it be like this, until she becomes pure. When she becomes pure, divorce her before having intercourse with her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is the way that Allah has decreed, women should be divorced accordingly."
"3911","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a divorce to his wife."
"3912","Nafee narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The woman was in the state of menstruation at that time. A narrator named Ibn Abi Zayb has narrated these words in a hadith: It was a divorce (the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace) said, \This is the way that Allah has decreed"
"3913","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam). She was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar asked the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) about this order (after that, he mentioned it according to the previous hadith)."
"3914","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to keep this woman with him until she becomes pure. The narrator did not mention Sayyiduna Umar in this tradition."
"3915","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “It will be one (divorce count)."
"3916","Jabir al-Thuq says: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: A person divorces a woman in the state of menstruation, so Sayyidna Ibn Umar said, \Do you know Ibn Umar?\"" He had divorced his menstruating wife. Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said: Tell him to go back to this woman"
"3917","Salma bin Abu Salama narrates about her father: It was mentioned before him that it is abominable to divorce three times at once, so he said, Hafs bin Amr bin Mughira had divorced Fatimah bint Qays three times with the same word, so we did not find any information that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, objected to him in this regard. Sath) had given three divorces, but no one objected to them either."
"3918","Sha'bi narrated: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave one divorce to his wife. The woman was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar inquired from the Prophet (peace be upon him) and told him about it, so he instructed him (i.e. Ibn Umar) to approach the woman and then divorce her again during her period of Idah."
"3919","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife and she was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, ``Abdullah divorced his wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet (PBUH) said, 'Tell her to return, and then when she becomes pure, her menses will come again after that, and when she becomes pure. Time, if he wishes, let him stay with her, and if he wants to divorce her, then he should not associate with her (rather divorce her). This is the way that Allah has ordered."
"3920","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of Sayyidna Dahhak bin Qays, narrates that she was the wife of a man from Banu Makhzoom, who divorced her three times and went away to participate in a war."
"3921","Salamah bin Abu Salamah narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Auf divorced his wife Tamazar bint Isbah Kalbiyah (her surname is Umm Salamah) three times with one word, so we did not find any information that anyone objected to him in this regard."
"3922","Salama bin Abu Salama narrates this statement of her father: Hafs bin Mughirah divorced his wife Fatimah bint Qays three times in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same word."
"3923","Along with another document, these two events are narrated together."
"3924","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates about Sayyidna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him: A man gave his wife a thousand divorces, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, three of them will be enough for you and leave the remaining ninety-eight."
"3925","Narrated Amr bin Murrah: I heard Mahan asking Saeed bin Jubayr about a person who divorces his wife three times, then Saeed said, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas was asked about a person who divorces his wife once, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, Through three divorces your wife will become forbidden to you and the rest will become a burden because you have mocked the verses of Allah."
"3926","Mujahid narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) asked about a person who gives his wife one hundred divorces. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas said: You have disobeyed your Lord and you have separated from your wife. You do not fear Allah, otherwise He would have created a place for you."
"3927","Mujahid narrates: A Qureshi came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and said: O Abu Abbas: I have divorced my wife three times in anger, then Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Abu Abbas cannot make it lawful for you that which has become haram for you. You have disobeyed your Lord and made your wife haram for you. He recited this verse: \And when you want to divorce women"
"3928","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and said: I have given my wife a thousand divorces. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Because of three divorces, your wife has become forbidden to you, and the remaining divorces have become a sin for you, because you mocked the verses of Allah."
"3929","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3930","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Divorce cannot be granted before marriage"
"3931","Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man cannot divorce, set free, sell, and fulfill a vow to what he does not own."
"3932","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man cannot divorce what he does not own, he cannot sell what he does not own, and he cannot free what he does not own."
"3933","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not permissible to free a man who does not own him. The narrator does not mention selling in it."
"3934","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever divorces something that he does not own, it will not be divorced, whoever frees something that he does not own, he will not be freed, whoever takes a vow about something that he does not own, his vow will not be valid, and whoever swears about a sin, his oath will not be valid, and whoever breaks it. If he swears about Rahmi, his oath will not be valid."
"3935","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Abu Sufyan bin Harb (may Allah be pleased with him) and instructed him: (i.e. the order is this) A man cannot divorce until he marries, and he cannot free what he does not own."
"3936","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) sent Abu Sufyan to the city of Najran in Yemen so that he could offer prayers, fight and receive charity there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised Abu Sufyan to have piety towards Allah, and this instruction states that no one can divorce a person with whom he has not been married, and no one can free him whom he does not own, and there is no status of vows regarding disobedience to God."
"3937","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was asked about a person who says: On the day I marry such and such a woman, she has a divorce."
"3938","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A vow is only about that which obeys the command of Allah."
"3939","Sayyiduna Muadh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Divorce can only be granted after marriage, even if the woman has been given a specific name. A narrator named Yazid bin Ayyad is weak."
"3940","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious and joking is also considered serious, divorce, marriage, and regression (i.e. return)."
"3941","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3942","Imam Zayd bin Ali (RA) narrates with reference to his ancestors: A person came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother mentioned to me a relative girl that I should marry her, so I said: If I marry this woman, she has three divorces. He said no, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then there is no problem. The narrator narrates that then the man married this woman."
"3943","Ibrahim bin Ubaidullah narrated this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A man among his elders gave his wife a thousand divorces, and his children came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, O Messenger of God: Our father has given our mother a thousand divorces. will be separated from him due to three divorces which are against the Sunnah and (remaining) ninety-nine divorces will be on his neck as a sin. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him) narrates that our teacher Ibn Abdul Baqi (apart from these two) all the narrators of this tradition are unknown and weak."
"3944","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) said to me: O Mu'adh, whoever divorces one, two or three times as an innovation (i.e. against the Sunnah), We will make his innovation obligatory on him. A narrator named Isma'il bin Abumiya al-Basri is an obsolete hadith."
"3945","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person (or about a person) who had divorced his wife, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said, “You people are mocking the verses of Allah. (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words) Playing with the religion of Allah, whoever divorces, We will make three divorces obligatory for him, and that woman will not be lawful for him until he becomes a widow or divorcee after the second marriage. The narrator named Ismail bin Abuamiyyah has a weak hadeeth."
"3946","Habib bin Abu Thabit narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and said: I have given my wife a thousand divorces. Sayyidna Ali said: Three divorces have made it haram for you, and you should divide the remaining divorces among your other wives."
"3947","Saeed bin Jubayr and Mujahid narrate on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: He was asked about a person who divorces his wife by the number of stars, then Sayyidna Ibn Abbas said: This person violated the Sunnah and his wife became forbidden to him."
"3948","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: A man divorced his wife as many as the number of stars, then Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said about him, This man violated the Sunnah and his wife became forbidden to him."
"3949","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \A pregnant woman"
"3950","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \A pregnant woman"
"3951","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a pregnant woman, a widow, that she will not get any expenses."
"3952","Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a woman who has been divorced three times will not get housing and expenses."
"3953","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to Fatimah (bint Qays) that the woman whose husband has the right to appeal to her will receive the housing and expenses."
"3954","Amir Shaabi narrates: We came to the service of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, and we said to her: Narrate to us the hadith in which the decision of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is mentioned. It is to say that I will not get housing and expenses, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will get housing and expenses. (His brother-in-law) said: Her husband has divorced her three times. Sha'bi narrates: When I came to Kufa, Aswad bin Yazid called me to ask me about this."
"3955","Aswad narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) found out about the statement of Sayyida Fatima Bint Qays (RA), he said, \We will not impose orders on Muslims because of the statement of a woman.\"""""
"3956","Shaabi narrates: Aswad bin Yazid met me and he said to me: O Shaabi, fear Allah and refrain from quoting the hadith of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays (RA), because Sayyiduna Umar (RA) has given such a woman the right to live and spend. The hadith was narrated to me."
"3957","Narrated Shaabi: I went to the service of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the decision of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she said: Her husband divorced her. She went to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He did not give the right to spend. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The woman whose husband has the authority to refer (to her) the residence and the expenses are given.\"""""
"3958","This tradition is narrated along with some other isnads, and in the tradition of Majalid, these words are: Housing and expenses are given to the woman whose husband can approach her."
"3959","Aswad narrates: When the statement of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) came to light, he said, \We will not abandon the commandments of the Book of Allah because of the statement of a woman"
"3960","Abu Ishaq narrates: I was sitting in the big mosque with Aswad bin Yazid. Sha'bi was also present with us. Sha'bi narrated this hadith regarding Sayyida Fatima bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give her the right to live and spend. He said: We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the commandment of the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the statement of a woman, because we do not know that this woman has forgotten (the original matter)."
"3961","Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My husband divorced me three times. Abu Ishaq narrates: When Sha'bi narrated this tradition, Aswad threw stones at him and said: You are the ones who are narrating this tradition or giving a fatwa on the basis of this tradition. We will not abandon the commandment of the Book of Allah because of the statement of a woman (that commandment is this): \Do not drive them out of their homes"
"3962","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3963","Abdullah bin Khalil Hazrami narrates: Sayyidah Fatimah bint Qays was mentioned before Sayyiduna Umar bint Khattab, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give her the right to live and spend. A narrator named Hasan bin Amara is obsolete."
"3964","Aswad narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Umar: We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the statement of a woman. Amish narrated this tradition from Aswad regarding Ibrahim and did not quote these words in it, and the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we have noted this tradition before: Amish is a more authentic and a greater Hafiz al-Hadith than Ash'at."
"3965","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3966","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife and she was menstruating at that time. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to go back to her and let her stay like that until she becomes pure. Then when she next menstruates, let her stay like this until she becomes pure. Divorce her first, this is the way that Allah Ta'ala has ordered, according to which women should be divorced. The narrator narrates: When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar was asked about this, he used to say, If you have given your wife one divorce (then you should return), because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to do so, but if you have divorced this woman three times, then she will remain forbidden to you at that time, until she marries another person (mutlaqah yabih). You have disobeyed Allah in this regard."
"3967","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife while she was menstruating. A narrator named Ibn Arfa narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife, she was menstruating at that time. After that, the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him (Ibn Umar) to approach this woman, then leave her alone until she next menstruates, then leave her alone until she is purified, then divorce her before having intercourse with her, this is the method that Allah Almighty has mentioned. He has ordered that women should be divorced accordingly. The narrator narrates: When Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was asked about a person who divorced his wife during her menstruation, Sayyidna Ibn Umar would say: If you have mentioned a divorce, then the Prophet (PBUH) has instructed about such a person that he should return to that woman, then let her stay like that until she next menstruates, then let her stay like this until she becomes pure. If you divorce her three times, then you have disobeyed what Allah commanded you about divorcing your wife, and your wife has separated from you without reason."
"3968","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and the woman was in the state of menstruation at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) asked the Prophet (SAW) about this order, and he said, Tell him to approach this woman (after that, the narrator mentioned the previous hadith). In this hadith there are these words: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said to such a person: If you have divorced your wife once or twice, the Prophet (PBUH) gave me this command."
"3969","Nafi' narrated: When a person asked Abdullah Ibn Umar about the issue of divorcing his wife while she was menstruating, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) would tell him what the Prophet (PBUH) had said, then he would say, \If you have divorced your wife once"
"3970","Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates this statement of Sayyida Fatima bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her. She was the wife of Abu Amr bin Hafs bin Mughirah, and she also divorced him for the third time. When she attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he inquired from him about this issue. Marwan did not accept that a divorced woman can leave her house, he did not accept the statement of Sayyida Fatima bint Qais as reliable. Narrated Urwa: Sayyida Aisha also did not accept the statement of Fatima bint Qays."
"3971","Uza'i narrates: I asked Zahri which wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge with you. So they replied, Urwa bin Zubair told me about Sayyida Aisha that this woman's name was bint Jun Kalabiya, when they visited her and got close to her, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: You have taken refuge in a great person, go to your family."
"3972","Suwayd bin Ghafla narrates: A woman named Aisha Khatamiyyah was the wife of Sayyidna Imam Hass bin Ali (RA). When Sayyidna Ali (RA) was martyred and allegiance was given to Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA), this woman said: Amir al-Mu’minin, may you be blessed with the Caliphate. Narrated by the narrator: This woman wrapped her veil, until when her Eid was completed, Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (RA) gave her the rest of her dowry and ten thousand (dirhams or dinars) as a dowry. The woman said: These things are very little compared to the beloved who is parting. Hada, (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) My father (Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me. Be done. (Imam Hasan says:) Then I would turn to him."
"3973","Suwayd Bin Ghalfah narrates that when Sayyidna Ali (RA) passed away, Aisha bint Khalifa Khatamiyyah, who was the wife of Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA), said to Sayyidna Imam Hassan (RA): Congratulations on becoming the Commander of the Faithful, then Sayyidna Imam Hassan (RA) said to her: You are congratulating me on the martyrdom of Commander of the Faithful (i.e. Sayyidna Ali (RA)), go away, you are divorced. She put her cloth over her face and said: O Allah, my intention was only good (i.e. I did not have this intention). Later Sayyiduna Imam Hasan sent this woman ten thousand dirhams or dinars and the rest of the dowry as a reward. When these things were placed in front of her, she turned and said: All this is very little compared to the beloved who is being separated. A person who divorces his wife three times, such as one divorce in every tahr or one divorce in every month or three divorces at once, then that woman will not be lawful for that person until she marries another person."
"3974","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: He divorced his wife once, while the woman was menstruating at that time, then he intended to give the remaining two divorces to this woman during the subsequent purifications. Allah did not command you (to divorce) in this way. You have disobeyed the Sunnah. The Sunnah is that you should first purify her and then give her a divorce in each purification. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed me, so I turned to this woman. He said, O Messenger of Allah, what do you say, if I divorce her three times, will it be permissible for me to approach her? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No (in such a case) she will be divorced from you and (this method of divorce) will be a sin."
"3975","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: If a person divorces his wife three times, then she is divorced from him, and that person disobeys his Lord and has violated the Sunnah."
"3976","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Three divorces are made through Bariya, Batah, Bain, and Haram, and that woman will not be lawful for a man until she remarries (mutlaqah yawiah)."
"3977","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “When a man divorces his wife three times, that woman is not lawful for him until she remarries, and each of them (husband and wife) does not taste the honey of the other party.”"
"3978","Nafi bin Ajir narrates: Sayyidna Ruqana bin Abdazid (RA) divorced his wife, Suhaimah, then he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given divorce notice to my wife, Suhaimah. By Allah! Did you mean only one divorce? Sayyiduna Rukana (RA) said: By Allah, I intended only one divorce, so the Prophet (PBUH) sent that woman back. Sayyidna Ruqana (RA) gave this woman a second divorce during the caliphate of Sayyidna Umar (RA) and a third divorce during the caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
"3979","Nafi bin Ujair narrates: Sayyidna Ruqana bin Yazid divorced his wife Suhaimah. He told the Prophet about this. He said, O Messenger of Allah, I have divorced my wife Suhaimah. By Allah, I intended to give only one divorce through her. The Prophet asked Sayyiduna Ruqana. By Allah! Did you mean only one divorce? Sayyiduna Rukana (RA) said: By Allah, I meant only one divorce, so the Prophet sent the woman back. Sayyidna Ruqana (RA) gave this woman a second divorce and a third divorce during the Caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman (RA). Imam Dawood says, this hadith is correct."
"3980","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3981","Abdullah bin Ali, on the authority of his father, narrates this about his grandfather: He divorced his wife during the blessed covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: What did you mean by that? He said: A (divorce) The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: By Allah: He said: By Allah! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It will be according to your wishes.\"" In this hadith"
"3982","Abdullah bin Ali narrates: My grandfather Sayyidna Raqana bin Abd Yazid (RA) divorced his wife. He came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have divorced my wife. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What did you mean (by these words)? He said: I meant a divorce. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: By Allah! He said: By Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it will be one (divorce count). Ishaq ibn Israel has narrated a hadith to the contrary (which follows)."
"3983","Abdullah bin Ali narrates this about his grandfather Sayyidna Raqana bin Abd Yazid Radiyallahu Anhu: He divorced his wife, then he attended the Prophet's service and mentioned this to him. The Prophet inquired: By Allah! Did you just mean a divorce? He said: By Allah, I meant only one divorce. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it will count as one divorce."
"3984","Sayyidna Muadh Bin Jabal Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Muadhullah, the Almighty has not created anything on earth that is more pleasing to Him than freeing a slave, and Allah has not created anything on the earth that is more displeasing to Him than divorce. The right of exception will not be granted, if a person says to his wife that if Allah wills, you have divorce, then that person will have the right of exception and divorce will not take place."
"3985","This tradition is narrated along with another document. Hameed narrates, Yazid bin Haroon said to me: How great this hadith would have been if its narrator Hameed bin Malik Lakhmi had been known. I said: He is my grandfather. Taweezid said: You have made me happy, you have made me happy. Now this hadith has become (authentic)."
"3986","Narrated by Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Allah has not declared anything as halal, which is more distasteful to him than divorce."
"3987","Sayyiduna Abu Thalaba Khoshni (RA) narrated: My uncle said to me: You work for me so that I may marry my daughter to you. I said: If you marry my daughter to her, she will have three divorces. Then later I felt it appropriate to marry this woman. It can be given only after, so I got married to this woman and then Saad and Saeed were born to me."
"3988","Muhammad bin Ubaid narrates: Udi bin Udi Kundi sent me to Safiyya bint Sheebah to inquire from her about the traditions that she narrates with reference to the lady Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her), so this lady said, Saida Ayesha Siddiqa narrated to me that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ``Etaq (liberation of the slave) by force (by force) does not take place."
"3989","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates this saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \This divorce does not take place by force (through) Ataq (freeing the slave)\""."""
"3990","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas says: There are four ways of divorce, two of them are halal, and two ways are forbidden. As far as the two halal ways are concerned, that is for a man to divorce his wife while she is pure, without having intercourse with her, or he divorces his wife when she is pregnant and her pregnancy is obvious. Diede, or divorce her after intercourse with her, in which it is not known whether (as a result of this intercourse) pregnancy has been declared or not?"
"3991","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained that his master had married him and now he wanted a woman: separate him and his wife. Want to be careful! The authority to grant divorce is to be given to the one who holds the shank."
"3992","Narrated by Ikramah: A slave came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) (followed by the previous hadith) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right to divorce belongs to the one who holds the shin. The narrator did not mention (in his chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas."
"3993","Sayyidna Asma bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A slave came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, My master married me first, and now he wants to separate me and my wife."
"3994","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be two divorces (given to a maidservant) and her period of menstruation will be two."
"3995","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, Umar bin Shaib is unique in quoting this tradition as a marfu’, hadith. This is a weak narrator."
"3996","Salim states: A person who is a slave and his wife is a free woman, or a man who is free and his wife is a maidservant, whichever of the spouses is mamluk, then the divorce will be reduced due to this mamluk, however, the status of the woman will be considered in Idda."
"3997","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A slave (husband) can give two talaqs to a free (wife) and the woman's period will be three Qur'a."
"3998","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: When a free woman is the wife of a slave, then the woman can be given two divorces, and her iddat will be three menstruations, and when a slave girl is the wife of a free person, two divorces can be given to her, and her iddtah will be two menstruations as a slave woman."
"3999","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: When a slave divorces his wife twice, that woman becomes haram for him until she remarries (a widow or divorcee)."
"4000","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, says this about a slave girl who is the wife of a free man: She will become a widow through two divorces, and she will perform two periods of Iddah, and when a free woman is the wife of a slave, she will become a widow through two divorces and will perform three periods of Iddah. This hadith has been narrated by other narrators as a muqaf, tradition, and it is true that this tradition has been narrated as a marfu’ hadith with one and a chain."
"4001","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: I said to the Prophet (PBUH): \And the end of the period of pregnant women is that they give birth.\"" This ruling is for a woman divorced three times? Is it for Yabih? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is for the divorced and also for the widow."""
"4002","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The divorce of a slave will be two, and then that woman will not be lawful for him until she marries another (widow) and the maidservant's Idda will be menstruating."
"4003","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates this saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \A slave girl can be given two divorces and her Idda will be two menstruations. With another chain of transmission it is narrated that Sayyida Aisha says"
"4004","Abu Asim says: In Basra, there is no more, negative tradition than this tradition narrated by al-Mazahir."
"4005","Zayd bin Aslam narrates: Qasim was asked about the concubines, how many divorces can be given to him? He said that she can be given two divorces and her Idda will be two periods. The narrator narrates: He was asked whether any hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached you. He replied no."
"4006","Zaid bin Aslam narrates: Qasim was asked about the iddah of the maidservant and he said, People say it will be menstruation, we do not know about it (the narrator doubts or perhaps these are the words) We do not find this ruling in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger. Ibn Wahib has quoted the same saying of Qasim and Salim with his chain of command. This ruling is not in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, but Muslims follow it."
"4007","Ikrimah narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Using the word haram (for a wife) is not divorce, but an oath for which expiation must be paid. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about using the word Haram, this is an oath for which expiation will be paid. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) says that the best example for you is in the life of the Prophet (PBUH). \Why do you declare that which Allah has made lawful for you: \""This verse is even here"
"4008","Hisham said: Yahya wrote to me from Ya‘la ibn Hakim, from Sa‘id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ‘Abbas, that he used to say: “In [the matter of] the haram [oath], it is an oath that requires expiation.” And Ibn ‘Abbas said: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have a good example (Qur’an 33:21), that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade his concubine to himself, so Allah said: ‘Why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you?’ (Qur’an 66:1) until His saying: ‘Allah has already ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths’ (Qur’an 66:2). So he expiated for his oath and made the haram an oath.”"
"4009","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a person declares his wife haram for him, this oath will count and that person will pay expiation for the oath. Sayyiduna Ibne Bass (RA) said, \There is an excellent example for you in the life of the Prophet (PBUH)."""
"4010","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: If you use the word Haram, you will have to pay Kaffara."
"4011","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (SAW) on the authority of Sayyidna Umar (RA)."
"4012","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Using the word haram is an oath for which expiation will be paid."
"4013","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA): Once, the Prophet (PBUH) came to the house of Sayyida Hafsa (RA) along with his mother, Sayyida Mariya Qobtiyya (RA). You have done this to me by leaving your other wives, because \I have no status in your eyes.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said"
"4014","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Hafsa (RA) found the Holy Prophet (SAW) with Umm Ibrahim (i.e. Sayyida Mariya Quptiya (RA)) on the special day of Sayyida Ayesha (RA), so she said: I will definitely tell (Sayida Aisha) about this. Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) told about this to Sayyida Ayesha, then Allah told His Messenger about it. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been informed by one who has knowledge and information. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with his wives for a month, then Allah revealed this verse. \If both of you repent before Allah (it would be appropriate) because both of your hearts were crooked.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I asked Sayyidna Umar (RA)"
"4015","Ata says: Whoever says to his wife: You are forbidden to me, you are forbidden to divorce, you have a harmful divorce."
"4016","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that a man came to him and said: I have declared my wife forbidden to me. \O Prophet! Why do you make that thing haram"
"4017","It is narrated about Sayyidna Rafi bin Sinan (RA) that he accepted Islam but his wife refused to accept Islam. They had a little girl who had reached the age of weaning. They both came to the Prophet (PBUH) with their case. Waslam prayed, O Allah, grant her guidance, then the girl turned towards her father, then Sayyidna Rafi' (RA) obtained her."
"4018","It is narrated about Sayyidna Rafi bin Sinan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he accepted Islam, his wife refused to accept Islam, they had a daughter, whose name was Umayra, the woman asked for the child, then Sayyidna Rafi, may Allah be pleased with her, refused. Both of you call this girl, both of them called, the girl started to turn towards her mother, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, O Allah, guide her, then the girl turned to her father, so he got her, and took her with him."
"4019","Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahba came to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas said to him, Present your position (or question) and what is in your mind and what you have collected. Abu Sahba said to him: Do you know? In the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), three divorces were counted as one, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) replied, Yes, during the time of the Prophet (PBUH), during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA), and in the early days of the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (RA), three talaqs were counted as one. Done)."
"4020","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: O Moaz! Whoever divorces his wife one, two, or three times in an innovation (i.e. against the Sunnah) way, We will make his innovation obligatory on him."
"4021","Narrated by Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: O Mu'adh! Whoever divorces his wife for one time as an innovation, We will make his innovation binding on him."
"4022","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Whoever divorces his wife three times while she is menstruating, she will be divorced from him, but this person has disobeyed his Lord and violated the Sunnah."
"4023","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4024","Aban Ibn Taghlib narrates: I asked Imam Jafar Sadiq about such a person: who divorces his wife three times. Imam Jafar Sadiq said that woman will be divorced from that person and it will not be lawful for him until she marries another (widow or divorcee). So they answered yes."
"4025","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called Khulaa as a divorce."
"4026","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit Bin Qays (RA) had taken away her Khul from him, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed her to perform one period of menstruation."
"4027","Ikramah narrates: Thabit's wife (after her, according to the previous hadith) has mentioned (in her chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him)."
"4028","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: In the first two years of the Caliphate of the Holy Prophet (SAW) of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA), three (talaqs) were counted as one. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people have started hastening about what was given to them."
"4029","Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): Do you know that during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) during the caliphate of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and in the (initial) three years of the time of Sayyiduna Umar RA (RA) three (divorces) were counted as one. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) replied yes."
"4030","Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, I am asking you by Allah, do you know this? In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three (talaqs) were counted as one in the early period of the Caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar, so Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said yes."
"4031","Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, I am asking you by Allah, do you know this? In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three (talaqs) were counted as one in the early period of the Caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar, so Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said yes."
"4032","Ibn Abu Malikah narrates: Abu Jozaa said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: Do you know that three divorces were counted as one in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) (during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr) and in the early period of the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), so he (Ibn Abbas) replied yes."
"4033","Ibn Abu Malika narrated: Abu Jozaa said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: Do you know that three talaqs were counted as one in the time of the Holy Prophet (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr) and in the early days of Sayyiduna Umar?"
"4034","Mujahid narrates: One day I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, have I divorced my wife three times? Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: You disobeyed your Lord and your wife became forbidden to you. You do not fear Allah, otherwise He would have made room for you. Allah Ta'ala has said: \O Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! When you divorce women"
"4035","Mujahid narrates: A person asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, he said: He has divorced his wife three times, (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
"4036","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4037","Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says about Ela: After four months, it will be suspended (at the man's will) either he turns to it or applies it."
"4038","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4039","Suhail bin Abu Salih narrates this statement of his father: I asked 12 Companions about such a person who commits adultery, and they gave the same answer."
"4040","Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: I found ten companions of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with them) all of them say that they are suspended by the will of the one who gives them permission."
"4041","Taus narrates that Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) used to question the one who made the request."
"4042","Sayyiduna Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, did not think anything (i.e. divorce does not take place) even if four months pass (the issue of divorce at the will of the man)."
"4043","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) say: When four months have passed, it will be counted as a divorce."
"4044","Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) and Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) say: When four months have passed, it will be counted as a divorce."
"4045","Maimoni narrates: I mentioned to Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal the narration of Ata Khorasani on the authority of Abu Salama, narrated by Sayyiduna Uthman (may God be pleased with him), and he said, \I do not know what it is.\"" Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) has been quoted to the contrary. He was asked: Who copied it? He quoted the opinion of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding taws by Abd or Habib bin Abu Thabit."""
"4046","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) says: (in Ela) when four months have passed, it will be considered as a divorce, and the man will have the right to approach her until the woman's period is completed."
"4047","Ayyub narrates: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr: Did Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say: When four months have passed, it will be considered as a free divorce and Idda will not be required on the woman, she can marry (immediately afterwards) if she wants."
"4048","Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, narrated the following saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: When a woman claims that her husband has divorced her, and she also presents a just witness, then the husband will be sworn."
"4049","Narrated Abdullah bin Abu Malikah: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) about a person who divorces his wife without permission and then dies during her ``Idda''. So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) said: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Auf divorced his wife Tamazar bint Asbagh Kalbi, then Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA) died during this woman’s Idda, so Sayyidna Uthman (RA) declared this woman as an heir."
